### 20/cvss20.go
Masked section 1:
```
- **Required interface:** `func ParseVector(vector string) (*CVSS20, error)` — exported, package-level function. Consumed externally by a `package main` probe that imports `gocvss20 "github.com/pandatix/go-cvss/20"` and calls `cvss, err := gocvss20.ParseVector(v)`, and by the package'"'"'s own unit and fuzz test files (`package gocvss20_test`). The function must return a `*CVSS20` (the embedded-struct type declared elsewhere in this file) and an `error`. It must also be callable by the rest of this file, which calls `cvss20.Set(abv, v)` on the constructed value; `Set` is an exported method of `CVSS20` declared elsewhere in the file.
- **Observable behavior:** Parses a CVSS v2.0 vector string into a populated `*CVSS20`. The temporal and environmental metric fields are initialized to `"ND"` before any input is applied, so only the metric groups present in the input overwrite those defaults. The function consumes the input'"'"'s parts in a fixed, predetermined metric order: base metrics (`AV`, `AC`, `Au`, `C`, `I`, `A`), then temporal metrics (`E`, `RL`, `RC`), then environmental metrics (`CDP`, `TD`, `CR`, `IR`, `AR`). On success the returned `*CVSS20` is non-nil and the error is `nil`; on any error the returned pointer is `nil`.
- **Inputs:** `vector` — a `string`. The function splits it on `/` into parts and splits each part on `:` into an abbreviation and a value.
- **Outputs and errors:** On success, `(cvss20, nil)` where `cvss20` is a `*CVSS20` holding the parsed metric values with temporal/environmental defaults of `"ND"`. Errors returned (all with a `nil` pointer): `ErrTooShortVector` when the part count is not exactly 6, 9, or 14; `ErrInvalidMetricOrder` when a part'"'"'s abbreviation does not match the expected abbreviation at its position; and the error returned by `Set` (the value-validation error, `ErrInvalidMetricValue`, or `&ErrInvalidMetric{Abv: abv}`) when a metric value is rejected. The error identifiers are declared in `20/errors.go`.
- **Side effects and interactions:** Calls the exported `(*CVSS20).Set(abv, value string) error` method for each parsed metric to store its value. References the error values `ErrTooShortVector` and `ErrInvalidMetricOrder` from `20/errors.go`, and the types `CVSS20`, `Base`, `Temporal`, `Environmental` declared elsewhere in this file. Uses `strings.Split` and `strings.Cut` from the standard library.
- **Required sequencing and state:** Part count is checked first; only then is the `CVSS20` constructed and metrics applied. Within the ordered consumption, each part'"'"'s abbreviation is compared against the expected position before its value is stored; the first mismatch or the first rejected value aborts the parse immediately with the corresponding error, returning a nil pointer. The expected abbreviations form one ordered sequence — the base group'"'"'s, then the temporal group'"'"'s, then the environmental group'"'"'s — and each consumed part advances the expected position one step along that sequence.
- **Region boundary:** Self-contained. The range spans the entire `ParseVector` function declaration from its `func` line through its closing `}`; the replacement must provide a complete, syntactically closed function definition.
```

